WEBVTT

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:04.600
Hiroshima is the land without honor and humanity.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.770
Hiroshima

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:11.110
Nayotake Moonlight, its chivalrous vigilante squad, protected it for many years,

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.820
until its members began fighting over the rights of succession.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.990
In the midst of the bickering between its head and branch families,

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.290
the squad weakened, and public order deteriorated.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.460
Die, ya bastard!

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.000
Capture or be captured!

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.420
I'll tear ya to pieces!

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.760
Ya won't win this! Not in this lifetime!

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.930
As the curtain fell on the old days, a single girl appeared.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.440
Spitting on the yakuza ways of chivalry,

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:52.070
the pirate girl gathered the reckless and seized control of Okonomiyaki Village.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:57.450
She is the captain of the Ishizukuri Stones, Ishizukuri Shima!

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.990
License

00:00:58.990 --> 00:00:59.950
On the other hand, the Nayotake family, formerly the head household,
License

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:02.450
On the other hand, the Nayotake family, formerly the head household,

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.710
now can barely preserve their name in their little corner of the village.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.790
In fact, they were even facing eviction.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.590
I feel like I'm going crazy

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.350
I like nice songs

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:26.810
and I want you to listen to them too

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.770
Whenever

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:37.450
I sing a song

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.030
I hear a voice coming from the microphone

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:43.450
wishing me the best

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.200
I want you

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.750
to hear it too

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:48.580
Good luck!

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:52.750
You can't show your love

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:58.260
just with niceties

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.140
That won't provide comfort

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.520
Whenever I say something

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.610
out of the ordinary

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.900
in my heart

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.400
I wish you the best

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.950
I want you

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.580
to hear that line

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:24.580
Good luck!

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.810
Uu, wait!

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.180
Here!

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:48.810
Jeez!

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.070
I'd really like to get going to Hiroshima...

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.700
We're going to an okonomiyaki shop, right?

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.370
Yeah, and they sounded kind of desperate.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.330
Nonsuke!

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.330
Huh?

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.260
Hey, you!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.750
It's so pretty...

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.380
It's like a planetarium.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.760
It'll be a full moon soon.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.470
There's only one stop left on the peacebroker's list, huh?

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.970
I really wasn't planning on going with you the whole way.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.890
If only Nozomi hadn't held back again at Kyoto.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.900
The stone? I couldn't take that!

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.730
You were the one who launched the missiles, Ai.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.520
I didn't mean any harm...

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.070
Besides, it made the festival more exciting, so I'm sure we deserved at least one!

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.570
They sure are common for something that's supposed to be valuable, huh?
Besides, it made the festival more exciting, so I'm sure we deserved at least one!

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.160
They sure are common for something that's supposed to be valuable, huh?

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.410
But they said the stones are bad for your health.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.790
That's just some Kyoto crazy talk.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.420
It'll all be over soon...

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.540
Huh?

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.050
Nothing.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.720
All right, let's go to sleep!

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.510
We're leaving at 6 a.m. tomorrow!

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.390
But that's so early, Nozomi!

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.310
So, where is Chiaya?

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.270
Unfortunately, I still don't know.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.400
All I know is that she entered Okayama.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.780
You're lying.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.950
Huh?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.160
You're lying, aren't you?

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.450
I apologize.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.450
What are you trying to do?

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:17.170
First you let her get a license,
then you bought her a motorcycle...

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.830
I only gave her my old bi—

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:20.670
That's not the point.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:25.220
I understand where you're coming from, but she seemed so pitiful.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.970
She seems to have adapted to her surroundings, and above all,

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:34.770
I've never seen Miss Chiaya having so much fun.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.270
The next full moon is almost here.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.020
It only occurs once every 415 years!

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.110
I understand that.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.610
Gather as many stones as you can as soon as possible,

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.160
and bring Chiaya...

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.240
back.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:55.080
I understand.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:16.930
Hmph, that fox of a man.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.940
What did Shuten Doji do?

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:21.270
He's asking for more per stone.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.860
Looks like he won't join the project, either.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.070
That sounds like him, all right.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.610
They're here, Captain.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.710
Thanks for the deals as always, boys.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.580
Scope out the target yet?

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.380
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.540
Who's taking command?

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:46.590
I, Otomo, will personally oversee the operation.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.220
Very well.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.550
The hidden room seems to be in the basement.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.470
Oh? Lovely.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:24.920
Aw man, it's already noon!
Thanks for oversleeping, Ai!

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.050
You went back to sleep too, Nozomi!

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:30.010
Anyway, I didn't even eat breakfast, so I'm <i>starving</i>!

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:31.340
You big baby.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.640
Ah, that's more like it!

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.640
All right, let's get this show on the road!

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:44.520
Hold up—their famous kibidango! The show's gonna have to wait!

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.310
I almost missed it!

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:49.820
Let's eat!

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.780
Hey, Yukippe...

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:58.700
How can you all bear it?

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.500
Bear what?

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.910
That... you know...

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.630
When you change because you're not thinking...

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:10.010
You shouldn't show others that, right?

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.550
Change... what?

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:18.510
But we're BFFs, so it's okay.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:33.400
These are smaller than I expected.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:40.080
Ai, you never feel bad about eating the last one, huh?

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:41.870
Huh?

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.250
Oh, did you want it?

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.290
It's fine...

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.750
Oh, I would've let you have it if you said something.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.090
I said it's fine!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:55.340
What's your problem?
You should've just eaten it first.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:59.390
Ai, you're too selfish.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:00.260
Huh?

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:02.390
If you hadn't played so much at the beach,

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:05.560
you wouldn't have overslept,
and we'd be in Hiroshima by now.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:08.310
What does that have to do with anything?

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.150
Besides, you were playing, too.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.190
Th-That's true, but...

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:17.030
Anyway, isn't it kind of unfair to bring it up after the fact?

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.910
B-But you're always like that, Ai!

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.120
Like what?

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.580
Like... you know, like...

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.670
Oh, forget it.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.000
I'll go buy another one.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.420
That's not what I meant!

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.760
Let me ask you something.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:39.510
What makes you think you can boss us around like that, Nozomi?

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:40.350
Huh?

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:44.810
I don't remember signing up to be your lackey.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:47.020
You're kind of irritating sometimes.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.570
Come on, you two...

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.690
Uu, be nice.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.530
Nonsuke, you can have mine!

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.780
Well, <i>I</i> don't remember signing up to be <i>your</i> chauffeur.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.870
Okay, <i>sorry</i> for not having my license!

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.870
But I look at the map instead! Sometimes...

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.250
Sure, and then you either pass out or get us lost!

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.080
I'm not as bad as Yukina!

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:18.510
I thought you were more honest and heroic than that, Ai.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.180
What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:23.470
After you learned of the stones' power in Tokyo, it's become all you care about!

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:26.810
You're trying to get power the cheap, dishonest way!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:30.150
Th-Then <i>all</i> the Bests are dishonest!

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.060
If you really wanted to be that Maccha person's substitute,

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:35.480
then you should've become a Best from the beginning.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:40.360
Even if a Rest tries her best,
she'll never get anything done!

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.370
That's not...

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.750
Uu, where are you going?

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.830
I'm gonna look by myself.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.080
Later.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.510
Nonsuke, Uu's going to leave!

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:00.840
Let her go.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.890
I wouldn't want to <i>irritate</i> her.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:12.520
Let's move on.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:19.400
Oy, where's yer buddy?

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.150
How'd you know about her?

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:24.870
I got eyes, li'l lady. Looks ta me four o' ya been together fer some time!

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:28.580
Didja get in a fight? "Without honor and humanity"?

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.910
Th-That's not how it is...

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.290
Uu's not here...

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:36.130
Well, this here's the land without honor and humanity.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:41.260
Get yer fill o' okonomiyaki and momiji sweet buns and skedaddle, ya hear?

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.230
Nayotake
Bamboo
Nayotake
Bamboo

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.440
I guess this is the place...

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:00.650
Hello?

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:01.400
Welcome.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.610
Welcome!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:08.030
Um... Are Ponta, Yasu, and Tsune here?

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:13.830
We've got some young 'uns by them names. And you are?

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.420
Seconds, girls?

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.840
Kuramochi, they couldn't possibly finish any more.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.800
Oh, don't worry! One of us loves to eat...

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.440
Never mind that. We're fine.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:38.690
Eat as much as you'd like.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:41.440
It's to thank you for coming from so far away.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:47.570
They probably wanted Maccha Green to help with a raid.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:48.660
A raid?

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.660
It's a surprise attack.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:59.000
In the past, a chivalrous yakuza family called Nayotake hung their crest here.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:04.590
It was also the headquarters of the state vigilante squad, the Nayotake Moonlight.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:06.220
That's...
License

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:08.590
Circumstances forced them to give up control.
License

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:13.850
Pirates calling themselves the Ishizukuri Stones are trying to get that license.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:20.730
They're trying to force us out to pave the way for a new landmark for Okonomiyaki Village,

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.110
and Hiroshima's head of state has no plans to stop them.

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.280
Huh?

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.950
What about honor and humanity?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.450
They cannot stand in a village as bitter and foul as this.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.790
However, this young lady before you has had a good upbringing.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:36.290
It's high time we got out of here.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.620
Yet this is so delicious...

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.090
Do you want more takoyaki?

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:43.840
Yeah!

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:45.090
All right, here it comes!

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:51.100
Um... Is there anything we can do?

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:54.140
We accept your sentiments gratefully.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.520
I believe the letter said this stone was your payment.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:03.610
Oh...

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.980
Core...

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:06.530
But...

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:07.990
Pardon the intrusion.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:08.530
Welcome.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.160
Welcome!
Welcome.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.370
Momiyama?!

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:12.240
Huh?

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.490
Excuse me.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.870
Miss Chiaya, there is something I must tell you.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.250
Oh, ten orders of pork okonomiyaki and three bottles of ramune soda, please.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.930
Shigyo, how are you doing?

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:33.550
They said I can leave once this is off.

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:36.180
Is she still in bad condition?

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.730
She's faking it?

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.600
Her injuries are already healed,

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:43.690
but she apparently refuses to be discharged.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.020
Why not?

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:48.320
Isn't it obvious? Because she lost her stone.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:54.330
If it got out that Madam Shigyo is no longer a Best,

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:59.210
all the people she's beaten up will try and exact revenge.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.670
I'll do something about that.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.550
President Misono probably has some stones...

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:08.630
The president?

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:10.340
She seems to be gathering them.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:15.260
She asks for stones when I work as a peacebroker, too.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:18.980
She's gathering them? There are that many of these stones?

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:24.400
At the very least, there are as many as there are Bests.

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:27.610
What in the world are they?

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:29.860
I don't know.

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.360
All I know is that they're mysterious stones that fall from the sky...

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:41.410
The president of Tokorozawa's chief secretary...

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:45.130
So Chi was the daughter of the president, huh?

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:48.710
Your mother's worried about you.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:50.510
I'm not going home yet.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:53.300
How did you know about the Cores?

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:57.930
I heard you and Mom talking about them.

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.970
You said you needed to gather a lot.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:04.400
I found one, too, so I wanted to give it to her.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:07.320
You wanted to gather a lot?

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:11.610
Yeah. But if we got the stones, then the trip would end,

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:13.700
so I changed my mind.

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.910
Hey, Momiyama.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:21.540
Do those stones really let people become Bests?

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.540
Why does Mom want them?

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:24.670
Miss Chiaya.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:29.750
Please listen carefully to what I have to say.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.300
Thank you very much!

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.680
I have arranged a place for you to stay tonight.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.260
Please wait there until I pick her up.

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:45.190
I entrust you with guarding the daughter of the president of Tokorozawa.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:46.690
U-Um...

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.940
By the way, where is the other girl?

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:53.400
Oh, we had a little fight.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.520
Hey, Fatcho, I came to switch with you.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.240
Momiji Island Ferry
Momiji Island Ferry

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.740
Are you worried about that store?

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:44.540
Nonsuke, Yukippe. Go on ahead.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.330
I'm going to look for Uu.

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:47.620
Chi!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:48.370
Chiaya!
Chi!

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:53.880
Chiaya, what are you doing there?

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.670
But you didn't come home...

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:59.510
Didn't I tell you I'm busy every day?

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.390
Come on, clean that up.

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.720
Only if I can go to school!

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.560
Study with the teachers at home.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:09.150
You have a delicate constitution, so you can't—

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:11.020
I want friends!

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:15.360
You have Momiyama.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.110
Momiyama's old!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:23.740
Mom, this—

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.290
Sorry, Chiaya.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.540
Can this wait until later?

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.880
<b>The promise made by
four girls one summer...</b>

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.550
Mom, you know what?
<b>The promise made by
four girls one summer...</b>

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:41.550
I made friends.

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.390
Okayama
Okayama
